=== APPROACH ===
Manifest record (apps/parity/parity-manifest.json → page:power-user/Dashboards): requiredCount=16 =
  2 panels (GlassPanel1, GlassPanel2) + 1 state (success) + 13 strings (powerDashboards.*). 0 charts, 0 maps,
  no API data sources (renders from local state).

Composition (mirrors the sibling A7 pages):
  - DashboardsPageModel.kt    — framework-free: Registration (route id/web path/slug), CuratedDashboardPanel +
                                CURATED_DASHBOARD_PANELS (verbatim web catalog) + sortedCuratedPanels(),
                                DashboardsCatalog (success payload), CopyStatus, ClipboardTarget seam,
                                evaluateCopyStatus() (the web handleCopy state machine), recordDashboardsOpened().
  - DashboardsPageViewModel.kt — BaseFeedViewModel; state: StateFlow<UiState<DashboardsCatalog>> = immediate
                                UiPhase.Content (the single declared "success" surface); draft + copyStatus flows;
                                updateDraft/clear/copy/recordViewOpened.
  - DashboardsPage.kt          — stateless @Composable screen + stateful entry; title + intro chrome, GlassPanel1
                                (editor) + GlassPanel2 (catalog); all labels via stringResource; a11y semantics.
  - DashboardsPageHost.kt      — DashboardsRoute + DashboardsPageHost.register() (PageHosts seam).
  - TeslaSyncApplication.kt    — DashboardsPageHost.register() wired at process start (NavHost registration seam).
  - DashboardsPageTest.kt      — off-device unit coverage (model + view-model state machine).

Documented divergences (Honesty Covenant #9 — recorded, not silent):
  - The web AINLDashboardComposer (the optional AI drafter rendered between the intro and the editor) is a
    SEPARATE parity unit — a shared-surface with its own string set + tests
    (apps/android/app/src/main/java/com/teslasync/shared-surfaces/AINLDashboardComposer). It is NOT in this
    page-shell unit's manifest record (panels=[GlassPanel1,GlassPanel2]; its strings are absent from the 13). Out
    of scope here; not a scope narrowing of THIS unit.
  - The curated panel name/description pairs are technical reference data (the panel_name must match the Go
    catalog verbatim), hardcoded as literals in the web source too — NOT i18n strings, intentionally not in the
    13-string set. Reproduced as static Kotlin data (DashboardsPageModel.CURATED_DASHBOARD_PANELS).
  - DI: the app uses a manual LocalDataContainer + viewModelFactory seam (not Hilt). Followed the app convention,
    exactly like every sibling A7 page.
  - Draft persistence: the web localStorage draft maps to the view-model-retained draft (survives configuration
    changes). Cross-process persistence is not a manifest parity item and is out of scope (no DataStore/DI wiring).
  - editor.placeholder (the multi-line JSON example) is shown via the shared Textarea's `hint` slot, only while the
    editor is blank (mirroring the web placeholder that hides once text is entered) — the shared component models
    example text as a hint.

i18n (ADR-014):
  The 13 powerDashboards.* keys were missing from the web base catalog (web/src/i18n/en.json) because the web page
  used inline t() defaults. The Android catalog is GENERATED from the web catalog by
  apps/shared/i18n/generators/gen-i18n.ts (strings.xml is "do not edit by hand"). The repo was ALREADY in
  pre-existing i18n drift (committed strings.xml translated=7781 vs web 7975). To stay surgical:
    1. Added the 13 keys to web/src/i18n/en.json (source of truth — verbatim web defaults) so they survive any
       future regeneration.
    2. Ran the generator, then transplanted ONLY the 13 generated translation_powerDashboards_* entries into the
       three Android strings.xml (values, values-ar, values-he — ar/he carry the English fallback the generator
       materializes), reverting the unrelated regenerated drift (other Windows/.resw, Apple/.xcstrings, shared
       catalog, and the 194 pre-existing drifted keys) — keeping this change to the Android platform string catalog
       only. Each strings.xml gained exactly 13 lines (git numstat 13/0).
  lint disables MissingTranslation/ExtraTranslation (apps/android/app/build.gradle.kts), consistent with the
  English-fallback locale policy.

